1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,099
Doctors have nicknames for this one: "texting thumb" and "mommy thumb." Both point to the same thing — two tendons running through a narrow tunnel at the base of your thumb getting irritated, usually from one of three everyday habits.

2
00:00:10,419 --> 00:00:13,650
First, gripping your phone with one hand and scrolling with just your thumb.

3
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:19,076
That repeated spreading and bending motion inflames the tendon sheath until the tunnel gets even tighter.

4
00:00:19,396 --> 00:00:23,519
Second, a repeated gripping motion from racquet sports, weightlifting, or yard work.

5
00:00:23,839 --> 00:00:28,595
Doing the same grip over and over strains those same tendons, even if your phone habits are fine.

6
00:00:28,915 --> 00:00:31,965
Third, lifting and holding a baby with your thumb propping up the weight.

7
00:00:32,285 --> 00:00:35,030
Do that dozens of times a day, and it adds up the same way.

8
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:37,666
Hold your phone with both hands and switch your grip often.

9
00:00:37,986 --> 00:00:44,640
Warm up before gripping activities and switch hand positions, and support a baby's weight with your whole palm and forearm instead of just your thumb.

10
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:48,971
See a doctor if the pain lasts more than two weeks or the swelling gets worse.
